  "term": "social anxiety disorder",
  "definition": "Social anxiety disorder is an anxiety disorder involving an intense, irrational fear of social or performance situations where a person expects to be watched or judged by others. Being in these situations triggers anxiety, and adults typically recognize the fear as excessive or unreasonable.",
